                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Pencil Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>Studio Projects&#8217; C4 is a detachable-capsule pencil mic built by 797 Audio in China. The C4 is sold only as a matched pair.</p><p>Each mic has two three-way switches built into the body. The first is a three-position pad, offering 0dB, -10dB, and -20dB options. The second is a high-pass filter, offering a 6dB/octave cut at either 75Hz or 150Hz.</p><p><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/studioprojects/c4-original.jpg" class="thumb shaft" width="100" />Like most of the mics in the Studio Projects line, the C4 was redesigned in 2006 by Brent Casey of PMI Audio. According to Casey, the revised C4 has a new amplifier circuit designed for high headroom; the mic&#8217;s circuit can withstand 139 dB SPL with no pad, or 159 dB SPL with the optional non-capacitive pad engaged. </p><p>The new version also has higher sensitivity and 2dB lower noise (from 18dBA to 16dBA). Finally, a hypercardioid capsule was introduced.</p><p>The C4 kit includes a matched pair of head amps, two omni capsules, two cardioid capsules, two mic clips (p/n C4SC), two foam windscreens, a stereo mounting bar (p/n SPSB), and a hard-shell carrying case.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Studio-Projects/C4">Studio Projects C4</a> is also known as: C-4.</p><p>The mic was released in 2003.</p>
